#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0459 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0459 (Condition: TSVAL not populated with values or synonyms of values in the ISO 21090 null flavor codelist (or other terms that can be represented as null flavors); Rule: TSVALNF = null). Row 3: TSVAL carries a real value (AGEMAX=P85Y) and TSVALNF=NA is still populated -> fires. Row 1: real value, TSVALNF null -> silent. Row 2: TSVAL null with TSVALNF=NA, the condition does not hold -> silent. Row 4: TSVAL holds the null-flavor name UNKNOWN beside TSVALNF=UNK, a synonym of a null-flavor value -> silent. Partially executable: the open-ended "other terms that can be represented as null flavors" arm is not executable, only the ISO 21090 codes and their names are recognised."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 TSPARMCD=AGEMAX
dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
col TSVALNF  type=Char label="Parameter Null Flavor"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | AGEMIN | Planned Minimum Age of Subjects | P50Y | 
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | PCLAS | Pharmacologic Class |  | NA
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | AGEMAX | Planned Maximum Age of Subjects | P85Y | NA
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | REGID | Registry Identifier | UNKNOWN | UNK
